{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1251767-my-missing-pantheons","id":1251767,"title":"My Missing Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-05T14:57:45-07:00","id":1251767,"title":"My Missing Pantheons","content":"Could anyone provide information on the Imazighan, Pawnee, Malay, Miwok, Tehuelche, and Salish pantheons? I'd really like to use them, and I know of a couple gods for each, but info has proven quite scarce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 09-05-2018, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T16:26:36-07:00","id":1251784,"title":"","content":"No info, but many North Africans consider the name Berber to be derogatory since it has the Greek root as &quot;barbarian&quot; and has been historically used disparagingly. Imazighan (singular Amazigh) is their preferred name for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T18:28:17-07:00","id":1251800,"title":"","content":"Apologies. Thank you for the correction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T20:34:23-07:00","id":1251824,"title":"","content":"As far as I\u2019m aware, the Amazigh people are not known to have had a collective singular mythic tradition beyond a distinct trend toward ancestor veneration that continues today integrated into Islam in the form of honoring of the marabouts (over the violent objection of Wahabists).<br /> <br /> Before Islam, they took part part in the religions and collected elements from other peoples in North Africa, including the honoring of Egyptian gods, Hellenic traditions, elements of Judaism, and of course the Punic religion (worship of the Elohim gods of Carthage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T12:07:09-07:00","id":1257228,"title":"","content":"There's not really anything left of Berber/Imazi\u0263en mythology. I can't speak on the Pawnee and Salish, nor on the peoples of Malaysia.<br /> <br /> On the Tehuelche, however, you can begin with: Wilbert, Johannes Simoneau e.a. (ed.): <i>Folk literature of the Tehuelche Indians</i>. Los Angeles 1984.<br /> <br /> On the Miwok:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/dow/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/dow/index.htm</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/mim/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/mim/index.htm</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T08:21:08-07:00","id":1257371,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Looking through the Miwok texts, there seems to be quite a number of deities, which they refer to as the First People. I have no idea which ones would qualify as major gods or not, but there's the potential for a very sizable pantheon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Ah-h\u0101'-le</i> the Coyote-man</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>To-to'-kan-no</i> Chief of the Valley People, who became the Sandhill Crane</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Ah-wahn'-dah</i> Keeper of the Sun, who became the Turtle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Tol'-le-loo</i> the flute-player who became the White-footed Mouse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Wek'-wek</i> a Chief of the Valley People, who became the Falcon</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>We-pi-ah'-gah</i> a Chief of the Valley People, who became the Golden Eagle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Mol'-luk</i> who became the Condor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Hoo'-a-zoo</i> who became the Turkey Buzzard</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Hoo-loo'-e</i> who became the Dove</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Te-wi'-yu</i> who became the Red-shafted Flicker</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Wit'-tab-bah</i> Keeper of the Fire, who became the Robin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Hah-ki'-ah</i> who became the Elk</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Hal'-loo-zoo</i> who became the Antelope</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Sahk'-mum-chah</i> who became the Cinnamon Bear</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Le'-che-che</i> who became the Humming-bird</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Le-che-koo'-tah-mah</i> who became another small bird with a long bill.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Pe-t\u0101'-le</i> the Lizard-man</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Yu'-ka-loo</i> the Meadowlark-man</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Sah'-win-ne</i> the Hail Storm</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Nuk'-kah</i> the Thunder Shower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Os-so-so'-li</i> Pleiades, one of the Star-women</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Ke'-lok</i> the North Giant<br /> <br /> <i>Too'-le</i> the Evening Star, a Chief of the First People</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>He-le'-jah</i> the Cougar or Mountain Lion, another Chief, and partner of <i>Too'-le</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Kah'-kool</i> the Raven, who became a great hunter</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>To-lo'-mah</i> the Bobcat</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Yu'-wel</i> the Gray Fox</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Oo-soo'-ma-te</i> the Grizzly Bear-woman</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>O-woo'-yah</i> the Mother Deer</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T07:58:52-07:00","id":1257963,"title":"","content":"I know. They're on my list for the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T15:48:16-07:00","id":1258059,"title":"","content":"It's hard to find a full pantheon of Malay deities because of the spread of Islam and Christianity later on the peninsula. There's Raja Angin, the god of thunder and some Chinese Malay deities that are popular in the community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"htt